# =============================================================================
# ERP-Market multi-tenant reverse proxy (Caddy).
#
# The operator stack (deploy/docker-compose.yml) runs Caddy as the single
# entrypoint for ALL clients. Each client is exactly one site file:
#
#   deploy/caddy/sites/<slug>.caddy      (generated by scripts/add-client.sh)
#
# Caddy terminates TLS (Let's Encrypt via ACME, account email below) and
# proxies /api traffic to the client's API container over the shared
# `erp_proxy` Docker network:
#
#   Device (APK / browser)
#     │  HTTPS
#     ▼
#   Caddy :443 ──docker-DNS──▶ api-<slug>:3000 ──▶ db (per-client Postgres)
#
# No host ports are published per client — containers talk over the internal
# erp_proxy bridge by DNS name.
#
# sslip.io: until a real domain is configured, hostnames like
# <slug>.<VPS_IP>.sslip.io already resolve to this VPS, so each client gets
# real Let's Encrypt HTTPS with zero DNS work.
# =============================================================================

{
    email {env.CADDY_EMAIL}
}

# One site file per client (do not edit by hand — use add-client.sh):
import sites/*.caddy

# ── Example site (documentation only — real files are generated) ─────────────
# Custom domain:
# acme.erp.example.com {
#     reverse_proxy api-acme:3000
# }
#
# sslip.io auto domain (VPS IP, no DNS setup):
# acme.203.0.113.10.sslip.io {
#     reverse_proxy api-acme:3000
# }